.TH "nydus-client" "1" "May 2025" "Christopher Irving" ""
.SH "NAME"
.LP 
nydus\-client \- Client program which requests a Minecraft account from the Nydus Launcher server and launchers Minecraft with it. 
.SH "SYNTAX"
.LP 
nydus\-client
.LP
nydus\-client --version
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.LP 
When
.BR nydus-client
is invoked, it will attempt to contact a Nydus Launcher server to be allocated a Minecraft account and access token.
If successful, it will launch Minecraft using that account.
While running,
.BR nydus-client
will periodically renew its account allocation with the server.
Once Minecraft is closed,
.BR nydus-client
will again attempt to contact the server to release its ownership of the Minecraft account.

The only command line argument
.BR nydus-client
accepts is
.BR --version.
If given this argument,
.BR nydus-client
will simply print the version of the currently installed Nydus Launcher software
and exit, instead of performing its normal task of requesting an account and
launching Minecraft.

All configuration of
.BR nydus-client
is done by settings in the configuration
file found at
.IR /etc/nydus/nydus-client.conf.

See
.BR nydus-client.conf (5)
for details on the configuration file's format.

To run a Nydus Launcher server, see
.BR nydus-server (1).

.SH "SEE ALSO"
.LP
.BR nydus-client.conf (5),
.BR nydus-server (1),
.BR nydus-cli (1)
